```typescript
export function binaryFindPartition<T>(
    array: readonly T[],
    partition: (item: T) => boolean
): number {
    if (array.length === 0) {
        return -1;
    }
    let low = 0, high = array.length - 1;
    while (high > low) {
        const mid = low + Math.floor((high - low) / 2);
        if (partition(array[mid])) {
            high = mid;
        } else {
            low = mid + 1;
        }
    }

    return partition(array[low]) ? low : -1;
}
```

Rocky explain steps. First, check if array empty. If yes, return -1. Next, set low to 0 and high to last index. While high greater than low, calculate mid. If partition true for middle item, move high to mid. If not, move low to mid + 1. 

At end, check partition for item at low. If true, return low. If not, return -1. Good, good, good.

